We would like to confirm what course of action is required should there be changes in the work conditions as stated in the Offer of Employment submitted in support of LMIA-Exempt work permits. In particular, what action is required if:
1. There is an increase in salary;
2. The applicant is now receiving a bonus, but was not at the time the offer was submitted or was omitted in error;
3. The applicant is now receiving benefits but was not at the time the offer was submitted or was omitted in error;
4. There are changes in job duties listed in the Offer of Employment, for instance, the applicant still qualifies under the NOC code submitted in the Offer of Employment but may be working on a different project for the same employer or assume additional duties that may not have been listed;
5. The applicant temporarily leaves Canada while their work permit is valid, yet the Offer of Employment does not indicate that their work in Canada will be intermittent;
6. The applicant permanently leaves Canada while their work permit is valid.
If a response could be provided for each of the numbered items, it would be greatly appreciated.
Thank you in advance for your assistance and prompt attention to this matter.
Happy Holidays!
